From: Sergi Perich <info@soploslinux.com>
Date: 2026-10-19
Subject: [PATCH] drm/i915: make the driver usable on PREEMPT_RT

Mainline marks DRM_I915 as "depends on !PREEMPT_RT". Every PREEMPT_RT
kernel therefore silently loses the driver at "make olddefconfig", and a
machine with an Intel iGPU boots to a black screen and a blinking cursor
because no KMS driver exists for it.

The reason for the dependency is that i915 takes spinlock_t locks with hard
interrupts disabled, which is fine on a regular kernel and a sleeping-in-
atomic bug on PREEMPT_RT, where spinlock_t is a sleeping lock.

This patch removes the dependency and fixes the places where that happens:

  - Vblank evasion (intel_pipe_update_start/end, the legacy cursor update,
    the scanout position query and the evade loop) runs with interrupts
    disabled and calls into intel_vblank_section_enter(), which takes
    uncore->lock (needed on IVB and HSW to serialise register accesses).
    On RT the section now keeps interrupts enabled. Evasion becomes best
    effort: an atomic update preempted past its vblank shows up as an
    "Atomic update failure" for that one frame instead of sleeping in
    atomic context. Xe shares these files and is left unchanged.

  - The display tracepoints sample the scanline in TP_fast_assign, which
    takes uncore->lock. Tracepoint probes run with preemption disabled, so
    on RT the scanline is reported as 0.

  - execlists_dequeue_irq() disabled interrupts around a section that takes
    sched_engine->lock. On RT the lock serialises the submission and the
    tasklet is never reentered, so the interrupt disabling is skipped.

Everything else that disables interrupts in i915 only touches seqcounts or
lockdep state and needs no change. A non-RT kernel builds to the same code
as before.

Not handled: GEM_BUG_ON(!irqs_disabled()) in i915_request.c and the
in_atomic()/irqs_disabled() checks in intel_engine_cs.c and intel_guc.h.
The asserts are only built with DRM_I915_DEBUG_GEM. The other two are worth
revisiting for GuC platforms.

Soplos Linux patch -- not for upstream submission.
Applies to Linux 7.3.x. Compile-tested on 7.3.0 with PREEMPT_RT and
without, for both i915 and xe. Not boot-tested yet.
